gschem icons
============

Icons for gschem live here.  They are compiled into the gschem executable
(glib-compile-resources, driven from ../src/Makefile.am) and registered at
startup with

    gtk_icon_theme_add_resource_path (gtk_icon_theme_get_default (),
                                      "/org/geda/gschem/icons");

so they are found by ordinary gtk_image_new_from_icon_name() lookups.
Nothing is installed and no icon theme cache is involved.

Layout
------

The layout is exactly the one the hicolor icon theme specifies:

    <size>x<size>/<category>/<name>.png

GTK exposes resources added with gtk_icon_theme_add_resource_path() as if
they were part of the hicolor theme, so no index.theme file is needed.
The recovered set contains 16x16 PNGs. Original gEDA mirror and rotation
XPMs retain their native 24x24 size. The insert-image and window-new SVGs
scale from a 24-pixel design grid. Their resource aliases use 24x24/actions
so they also resolve without an installed hicolor theme. GTK scales all
icons to the requested size.

Naming
------

The names are the ones gschem/src/actions.c asks for.  Two families share
this directory:

  gEDA action icons   insert-net insert-bus insert-symbol select deselect
                      clone multi-clone attribute-attach attribute-detach
                      attribute-show-both attribute-show-name
                      attribute-show-value symbol-datasheet insert-arc
                      insert-attribute insert-box insert-circle insert-line
                      insert-path insert-pin insert-text

  gtk-*        GTK+ 2 stock icon ids, kept under their historical names so
               that the action table did not have to be rewritten:
                   gtk-new gtk-open gtk-save gtk-print gtk-undo gtk-redo
                   gtk-cut gtk-copy gtk-paste gtk-delete gtk-edit
                   gtk-zoom-in gtk-zoom-out gtk-go-up ... etc.
               Where gEDA has its own artwork for the same action
               (new, open, save, undo, redo, edit, copy, delete) the gEDA
               artwork is used instead of the GTK one.

  The eight names that appear in both families (new, open, save, undo,
  redo, edit, copy, delete) use the gEDA artwork under its gtk-* name, so
  the historical ids keep resolving to gEDA's own drawing.

Additive only: to add an icon, drop the PNG in the right directory and add
a <file> line to gschem-icons.gresource.xml plus a line to EXTRA_DIST in
Makefile.am.

Provenance
----------

  gEDA artwork: gschem/data/*-16.png (and gschem/bitmap/gschem-*.xpm,
                converted to PNG), copied in unchanged.  These are the
                original gEDA action icons, licensed GPL-2.0-or-later.
                They cover most actions: insert-*, select, deselect,
                clone, the attribute-* toggles, and the toolbar icons
                new/open/save/undo/redo/edit/copy/delete.

  Material Symbols: for the gtk-* stock ids that gEDA never drew its own
                artwork for (gtk-about, gtk-print, gtk-zoom-in, ...),
                icons come from Google's Material Symbols set, outlined
                variant, rendered from the 24px grid to 16x16.
                Generated by ./fetch-material-icons.sh, which records the
                exact icon name used for each gschem id.
                Licensed Apache-2.0,
                https://github.com/google/material-design-icons


Regenerating
------------

  The PNGs are committed, so an ordinary build needs no network access.
  To re-render the Material Symbols ones:

      ./fetch-material-icons.sh

  It needs curl and rsvg-convert, and skips files that already exist --
  delete one to force it to be re-rendered.  Afterwards add any new lines
  to gschem-icons.gresource.xml and Makefile.am (the lists are sorted).

Recovery and build checks
-------------------------

Recovered from refs/tags/BAD_with_good_icons. The generated C file is rebuilt
from the manifest and images, rather than copied from that tag. Registration
is explicit in gschem_icons_init(), before menus and toolbars are constructed.
The numeric array output of glib-compile-resources (--compiler=msvc) keeps
strict ISO C diagnostics enabled; this switch does not invoke MSVC.

Resource aliases also cover the GTK 3 names document-new, document-open,
document-save, document-save-as, document-revert, view-refresh, edit-clear,
and preferences-desktop-keyboard-shortcuts, using the recovered artwork.

The four gaps in the recovered set are now filled:

  object-flip-horizontal: unchanged gschem/bitmap/gschem-mirror.xpm
  object-rotate-left:     unchanged gschem/bitmap/gschem-rotate.xpm
  insert-image:          project SVG artwork, GPL-2.0-or-later
  window-new:            project SVG artwork, GPL-2.0-or-later

All non-NULL icon names in the current action table are bundled. Missing
artwork must still never prevent actions or their menu labels from being
created.

Run make -C gschem/src check to decode and look up every embedded icon at
16 and 24 pixels with filesystem icon search paths disabled. This test needs
a GTK display; Automake reports it as skipped if no display is available.

Fixed UI appearance
-------------------

The policy is compiled in via gschem/include/gschem_appearance.h: Adwaita,
normal light appearance, Sans 10, and the hicolor resource layout. Startup
sets GTK_THEME for this process before GTK initialization, then sets the
application's GTK settings and removes filesystem icon search paths. This
uses GTK's built-in widget theme, GTK's built-in fallback icons, and the
bundled gschem artwork, including the original 48-pixel application logo.
There is no runtime theme selector. Schematic colors remain independent.

The appearance regression check starts with a nonexistent GTK_THEME value,
then verifies the selected theme, dark preference, empty icon search paths,
and application/dialog/file-chooser icon decoding on the real default theme.

Scheme action coverage
----------------------

Documentation actions in gschem/scheme/gschem/builtins.scm also need bundled
artwork: help-browser (including GTK's -ltr/-rtl names), gtk-help, help-faq,
and web-browser. The project SVGs cover these names. The REPL action's
accessories-text-editor name uses the recovered gtk-edit artwork.

GUI icon policy (2026-10-20)
----------------------------

The active GTK applications are gschem and gattrib. gschem embeds its action
and application artwork; gattrib embeds its own application artwork. Both use
the fixed appearance policy in gschem_appearance.c, with no desktop icon search
paths. gattrib has text menus, so its commands do not require themed icons.
Older Tk-based experimental helpers do not request desktop icon-theme names.

GTK can request directional variants of action names, even when a source only
specifies the base name. Resource aliases cover help-browser and
applications-science, including -ltr and -rtl. The resource regression tests
load these names with filesystem theme paths removed. Do not fix missing
artwork by asking users to install a desktop theme: bundle the required icon
or alias it to suitable existing project artwork and extend the tests.

Checks:
  make -C gschem/src check
  make -C gattrib/src check
